A||N||10||nikao1||?? Engine cuts in mid-flight ??||||5||
Z||000000||nikao1||01-14-2000||01:23 PM||||Been having this strange phantom glitch.?!? While driving at full speed the engine just stops (which is kinda exciting when i'm in the fast lane). Had the electrical system checked-- and supposedly no problem.<P>Anyway, the glitch occurs after about 40 miles of driving and if lights and/or radio is on, usually sooner.  When the engine stops the lights are still on, as well as, the radio.  After the 1st time, it starts up almost immediately. But after every "glitch" its harder to start until it won't at all.  The glitch runs the battery down.<P>Thought it was the alternator(which was pretty burnt out) but after replacement... a few days later the glitch re-appeared. Realized the battery wasn't secure (didn't replace the plastic bracket). Noticed the battery would knock against the wire set between it and the engine. Secured battery and tightened wire set plug connection...  Glitch still occurs.  <P>Questionable Autozone battery had it tested several times before the glitch.  Always tested good (at Autozone).  Just replaced it.  <P>Shooting in the dark... anybody got a light????||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sage||01-14-2000||01:47 PM||||Am also shooting in the dark, but from having had similar problems, I would check the ign. mod., and the pickup coil. If your hotwire was grounding out somewhere, you wouldn't have any lights or electric at all. Might also recheck the connections at the alt. How's your fuel filter and pump?  Does the car have good power when it is running?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-14-2000||01:49 PM||||Shot in the dark. Fuel pump. If you have the v-6 there is a schrader valve just to the right(passenger side) of the plenum. After the engine dies, kill the ignition right away (leave steering wheel unlocked so you can steer). Then open the rear decklid and push a phillips head screw driver down on the schrader valve "pin". Carefull, if you do have fuel pressure, gas will spew out. If no gas comes out, we've narrowed it down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wwh0001||01-14-2000||01:54 PM||||If the engine just stops running and doesn't slow down it probably isn't a fuel related problem. Its an ignition problem. Your battery may be drained when you try to start it back up. When it won't start take a plug wire off and put it next to metal. Have someone crank the egnine to see if you have a spark. No spark; ignition problem. I would agree with Sage that the problem is probably your pick up or ignition module.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by wwh0001 (edited 01-14-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by wwh0001 (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||cmyokley||01-14-2000||01:55 PM||||niako1,<P>read my post on 01-14 at 11:45, I am having the same type of problem. I am at my wits end. As my post said I will drive my car several miles then the rpm will start going up and down then the car will shut down all together and not start for several minutes. I am inclined to believe with all I have alteady done it has to be in the wiring or the ECM.<P>If I find out I will let you know.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-14-2000||02:21 PM||||Shorted tach filter? Anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sage||01-14-2000||03:30 PM||||I think maybe Raydar has it!||||reg||1
Z||000007||87 Steve GT||01-15-2000||02:52 AM||||had sorta the same prob. w/87gt and it was my cat. clogging and then get cool inside there and would crank and run for 30 mmin then have the prob again.. I just cut off cat. and installed a straight pipe there instead...   lol   I just remembered looking at the lobor reciept thta i also had a Accel Dist. put on too... so maybe it is ignition??||||reg||1
Z||000008||nikao1||01-18-2000||11:22 AM||||Thanks guys -- as you probably guess the new battery didn't kill the glitch.  But thanks I think I see the light at the end of the tunnel -- but I'm about to move to Florida (Orlando) Don't have the time/funds to tend to it right away.  But I can't let my baby (Imani- my white 85GT) stay sick for too long||||reg||12
Z||000009||william_thorniii||01-18-2000||12:10 PM||||Sage and Raydar are most likely correct.  It sounds like electrical and that leads me to believe that it is the tach filter.  Rodney Dickman sells a replacement part for it as well.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000010||fierospeeder||01-20-2000||03:08 AM||||I know its not your battery.  Tuesday, on my tbird, after 20 miles of driving i was at a light and the car just died out on me.  Possible ignition module dying on me?  I tried starting the car and all i hear is the solenoid clicking.  Aka dead battery.  I guess the one year old trak auto battery didn't like me anymore.  I was lucky to have a murphys parts store across the street for me to replace the battery. And yes my alternator is pumping out 14 volts.<BR>Just an example of when your battery goes out.  And my car was pushed by a beautiful female police officer into a grocery parking lot.  ||||reg||1
